      "id": "increment.v1-verifier-resource-boundary-hardening",
      "state": "active",
      "correctionClass": "verifier-untrusted-input-unbounded",
      "observedProblem": "The legacy continuation and public verifier still execute repository-selected Git behavior, project repository-controlled diagnostic text into model context, and parse JSON or traverse repository trees without code-owned resource ceilings, so future green verification can depend on untrusted local configuration or resource exhaustion.",
      "hypothesis": "Removing Git execution from the legacy continuation projection, exposing only code-owned verifier state there, and enforcing deterministic JSON, traversal and diagnostic ceilings can close the known execution and denial-of-service boundary without changing product semantics or creating a runtime.",
      "falsifier": "The verifier cannot preserve deterministic authority validation and useful bounded diagnostics without executing repository-selected programs, projecting raw repository text, or accepting unbounded input and traversal.",
      "stopCondition": "Finite negative tests prove no Git execution in continuation, no raw verifier diagnostics in model context, bounded CLI and authority/evidence JSON input, bounded authority and residue enumeration, and bounded diagnostics; canonical verification passes and no installation, outcome claim or repository residue remains.",
